{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeupDrQWRC8uJZo8CugL5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n\n- **ShipmentController.kt:26-44** — `create()` endpoint exists; no confirm endpoint yet\n- **Shipment.kt:23-27** — `ShipmentStatus` enum defines CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt:15-26** — In-memory store with `save()`, `findById()`, `existsById()` methods\n- **ApiExceptions.kt:18-24** — `ConflictException` (HTTP 409) and `ResourceNotFoundException` (HTTP 404) are defined; error handling is centralized via `GlobalExceptionHandler`\n- **ApiError.kt:31-37** — `ErrorCode` enum defines closed set of machine-readable codes\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n\n1. Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses; `GlobalExceptionHandler` catches and wraps in `ApiError` envelope\n2. `ConflictException` → HTTP 409; `ResourceNotFoundException` → HTTP 404\n3. Successful responses default to 200 OK when returned directly from controller; 201 CREATED uses `ResponseEntity.status()`\n4. Tests use MockMvc, verify both status and error body shape (see OrderControllerTest.kt:59-74)\n5. Data classes are immutable; `repository.save()` replaces entire entity\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must add `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint (cannot avoid; ticket requires new endpoint)\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add tests for new confirm endpoint and edge cases (cannot avoid; ticket requires verification)\n3. **ApiError.kt** — Must add new `ErrorCode` for CANCELLED shipment rejection (cannot avoid; error handling requires machine-readable code)\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Breaking existing tests if confirm endpoint interferes with URL routing (unlikely, path is unique)\n- Idempotency semantics: retrying confirm on CONFIRMED shipment must not fail or change state\n- Concurrent updates to repository: in-memory store with ConcurrentHashMap should be safe\n\n**Open questions:**\n\n- For a CANCELLED shipment rejection: what `ErrorCode` name? (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE vs SHIPMENT_CANCELLED vs other?)\n  - **Decision**: The ticket doesn't name this, but following naming patterns (SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS), I'll use `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to indicate the shipment is in a state that conflicts with confirmation.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to `ErrorCode` enum. This code signals that a shipment cannot be confirmed because it is in CANCELLED status (409 Conflict).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`:\n   - Fetch the shipment by ID; throw `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)` if absent\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, \"Shipment '...' is cancelled and cannot be confirmed\")`\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED via `repository.save(shipment.copy(status = CONFIRMED))`\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return as-is (idempotent)\n   - Return the shipment (defaults to 200 OK)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — Create S-1, POST confirm, verify status changed and body returned\n   - `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds idempotently` — Create and confirm S-2 twice, verify second call returns 200 OK with CONFIRMED, no error\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — Write CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, POST confirm, verify 409 Conflict with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` — POST confirm to missing ID, verify 404 Not Found with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- **Merge CREATED and CONFIRMED into a single \"confirmed\" state**: Rejected because requirement explicitly names three distinct states and tests for distinguishing them.\n- **Add a `confirmShipment()` method to repository**: Rejected because the repository is a thin wrapper; business logic (state transition validation) belongs in the controller per existing pattern (see OrderController create logic).\n- **Use HTTP 200 vs 201 for confirm success**: Rejected 201 because we're not creating a new resource, we're transitioning state. Existing `create()` returns 201 CREATED; confirm returns 200 OK (the default).\n- **Different error code for CANCELLED vs other conflicts**: Rejected; SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE is general enough for future status-based conflicts and avoids bloat.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | HTTP | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | repo.findById(id) | repo.save(copy with CONFIRMED) | Shipment JSON | 200 OK | Direct return |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED (retry) | repo.findById(id) | None | Shipment JSON | 200 OK | Direct return (idempotent) |\n| CANCELLED → rejected | repo.findById(id) | None | Error envelope | 409 | ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Not found | repo.findById(id) → null | None | Error envelope | 404 | ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test 1 — State transition**: Verify CREATED→CONFIRMED happens and persists\n2. **Test 2 — Idempotency**: Verify double-confirm of CONFIRMED shipment succeeds with no change\n3. **Test 3 — Conflict**: Verify CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with correct error code\n4. **Test 4 — Not found**: Verify missing ID returns 404 with correct error code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":353,"cache_read_input_tokens":19298,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":353},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"n