ancelled, already confirmed, created→confirmed) with appropriate exceptions and idempotency. Follows existing naming, exception, and return patterns exactly.\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added four test methods covering all four cases the ticket names. Tests verify status codes and error body structure (error.code field), consistent with OrderControllerTest pattern.\n\nAll changes are narrowly scoped to the shipment confirm feature.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements satisfied.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST endpoint to confirm shipments with state transition (CREATED→CONFIRMED), \n              idempotent retry, rejection of CANCELLED and missing shipments.\n\nChanged       sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt\n              — Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code for CANCELLED conflict rejection.\n              \n              sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt\n              — Added POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint with four-case state machine:\n                * Not found → ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n                * CANCELLED → ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n                * CONFIRMED → Idempotent return (200)\n                * CREATED → Transition to CONFIRMED, persist, return (200)\n\n              sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt\n              — Added four test cases:\n                * confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status (state transition + response body)\n                * confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds idempotently (retry safety)\n                * rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409 conflict (error code)\n                * rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404 not found (error code)\n\nTests         Test 1 verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition and return body\n              Test 2 verifies idempotent retry (call twice, both succeed with CONFIRMED)\n              Test 3 verifies 409 Conflict with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code for CANCELLED\n              Test 4 verifies 404 Not Found with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code for missing ID\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test (from sample-service/)\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 17 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors\n              (4 new confirm tests pass; 5 existing shipment tests unchanged; \n               4 order + 3 customer + 1 app tests unchanged)\n\nNot done      None. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all ticket cases implemented and tested.\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3112,"cache_read_input_tokens":23851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3112},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2256fe32-563f-425f-9915-a167b4941446","uuid":"3b9f5f28-1c6e-4f2f-9756-97e8b0366f04","timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:12:09.169Z","request_id":"req_011CeupHK8vtaGFT2YLaKHjw"}
